# Redirect URLs (keep enabled):
#   https://b2bconecta-app-git-dev-b2bconecta.vercel.app/**
#   https://www.b2bconecta.com.ve/**
#   http://localhost:3000/**
#   http://127.0.0.1:3000/**
#   ve.com.b2bconecta.app://auth-callback
#
# === SMTP (confirmación + recovery) ===
# Sender: b2bconecta.ve@gmail.com
# Dashboard → Authentication → Emails → SMTP Settings
#   o: bash scripts/configure_supabase_smtp.sh staging|production
# Ver config/smtp.env.example
#
# Google Sign-In (Auth → Providers → Google):
#   Enable provider with Web Client ID + secret from Google Cloud.
#   Authorized redirect URIs in Google Cloud must include:
#     https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
#   App redirect URLs above already cover web + ve.com.b2bconecta.app://auth-callback
#
# Password recovery AND signup confirmation on web use PKCE: open the email
# link in the SAME browser (and same origin / app) where the action started.
#
# Email templates (Auth → Emails):
#   Prefer {{ .ConfirmationURL }} so RedirectTo from the client is honored.
#   Do not hardcode Site URL alone for confirmation links.
#
# Android:
#   Mobile builds use ve.com.b2bconecta.app://auth-callback (see mobile-*.env).
#   HTTPS App Links for /producto and /vitrina require fingerprints in
#   web/.well-known/assetlinks.json (currently empty until Play signing SHA-256
#   is filled). Auth mail deep links use the custom scheme, not HTTPS yet.
#
# Canonical DEV web origin in this repo:
#   https://b2bconecta-app-git-dev-b2bconecta.vercel.app
# (Not `dev-b2bconecta.vercel.app` unless that alias is also allow-listed.)
#
# Ver config/ENVIRONMENTS.md
